---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = "When NOT to Use AI Automation in Your Business | PresciaIQ Insights";
const description = "AI is powerful, but it is not the solution to every problem. Here are three scenarios where human intervention is still the better choice.";
const canonicalURL = new URL("/insights/when-not-to-use-ai-automation/", Astro.site).href;
const date = "2026-08-17";
const category = "AI Automations";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  "headline": title,
  "description": description,
  "image": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/og-image.jpg",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "PresciaIQ",
    "url": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "PresciaIQ",
    "logo": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "url": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/logo.png"
    }
  },
  "datePublished": date,
  "dateModified": date,
  "mainEntityOfPage": {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": canonicalURL
  }
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalURL={canonicalURL}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground py-24">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="mb-12">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-primary border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5">{category}</span>
          <time class="text-sm text-muted-foreground font-sans">{new Date(date).toLocaleDateString('en-AU', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })}</time>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6 leading-tight">{title}</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">{description}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none font-sans">
        <p>As an AI development company, we spend a lot of time telling clients *not* to automate certain processes. AI is a tool for operational leverage, but applying it to the wrong problem creates more friction than it solves.</p><p>First, do not automate broken processes. If your internal workflow is chaotic and undocumented, adding AI will only execute that chaos faster. You must standardise the process before you automate it.</p><p>Second, avoid automating high-stakes emotional interactions. While AI support agents are excellent for tracking orders or processing returns, they should not be handling complex complaints, high-value client negotiations, or sensitive HR issues. Empathy and nuanced judgment remain uniquely human advantages.</p><p>Finally, do not build custom AI if an off-the-shelf SaaS product already solves the problem perfectly. PresciaIQ builds custom automations for the gaps that standard software cannot fill. If a $50/month tool does exactly what you need, buy the tool. We build for the problems that require a bespoke fit.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-white/10">
        <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-2xl p-8 text-center">
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4">Ready to automate your operations?</h3>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-6">Book a scoping call with our team to discuss how custom AI automations can eliminate manual work in your business.</p>
          <a href="/start" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-primary text-primary-foreground font-semibold text-sm hover:shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(0,255,136,0.3)] transition-all duration-300">
            Book a Scoping Call →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
